  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">REG: ASIA WATER FUND I</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">REG: ASIA WATER FUND I. The overwhelming amount of investment required to meet the growing demand for water supply and sanitation in Asia, at a time when fiscal policies are strained by stimulus packages meant to counter the effects of the global financial crisis, will make it difficult for public sector in the the developing world to continue to support capital-intensive projects in the water sector in its own. The private sector will have to play a key role in creating and maintaining water infrastructure during the decades to come.

To that end, as an independent investment vehicle comprising third-party capital, the fund is targeting a financial engineering niche in the water infrastructure sector in which project engineering companies are selected based on skill level as opposed to a conventional business model in which engineering companies are selected based on ability and willingness to invest their equity in a project. With this model, the fund expects to generate superior investment returns and greater private sector participation. This initiative is bolstered by water sector regulation, which has been moving toward full cost recovery policies in Asia and the Pacific, with willingness to reduce surface water pollution leading to tariff increases. Pricing water services in this manner encourages water conservation, as well as yield returns that justify investing in water sector infrastructure. Private water investments, incorporating the objectives of helping to alleviate Asia&apos;s impending water crisis while making a sustainable return to investors, create a win-win solution for all stakeholders.</narrative>
  </description>
